# .envrc — direnv configuration
#
# direnv automatically activates/deactivates the Nix dev shell when
# you cd into this directory. No manual `nix develop` needed.
#
# Setup (one-time):
#   1. Install direnv:   nix profile install nixpkgs#direnv
#   2. Hook into shell:  echo 'eval "$(direnv hook zsh)"' >> ~/.zshrc
#                        echo 'eval "$(direnv hook bash)"' >> ~/.bashrc
#   3. Allow this file:  direnv allow
#
# After that, every time you cd into this directory, the Nix shell
# activates automatically (and deactivates when you cd out).

# Use the flake's devShell — this is the main directive
use flake

# Load .env file for secrets/local config.
# Variables in .env are available in the shell but NOT exported to child
# processes unless you prefix them with `export` in the .env file.
# dotenv_if_exists reads the file silently if it doesn't exist.
dotenv_if_exists .env
